# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here ends up in the
# image. Two categories matter beyond image size:
#
#   * Secrets. .env holds the master key and database password. Baking it into a
#     layer would put them in any registry the image is pushed to, and they would
#     stay there even if a later layer deleted the file.
#   * Host-built artifacts. .venv is a Windows virtualenv with absolute paths and
#     platform wheels; copying it in would shadow nothing but waste hundreds of
#     megabytes and confuse anyone who found it.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# Runtime data, never part of a build.
documents/
backups/
media/
staticfiles/

# Notes and planning material.
.instructions/
*.md
!README.md
